{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION / CAVEAT ON THE N=1 PILOT ABOVE — it may not have been a true provider comparison, and I should not have recorded it without checking this.\n\nWHAT I NOW KNOW. The Pass-1 finder does NOT run on `cfg.model`. `production_batch_runner.py:87-93` sets `cfg = replace(cfg, model=req.model_ladder[0])`, where the ladder comes from the gate YAML — `workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml:62-65` = `[claude-haiku-4-5, claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-opus-4-8]` — and the code comment states the size ladder \"escalates up from here\". Measured on a real Anthropic review of 281f: 41 calls on `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` and 1 on `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6`, i.e. Pass-1 escalated to opus and Pass-2/Pass-4 took the sonnet verifier downgrade. So on the Anthropic path the operator's requirement (Pass-1 opus, Pass-2/Pass-4 sonnet) already holds.\n\nWHY THAT THREATENS THE PILOT. Those ladder entries are BARE model names, and `config.py:333-341` maps the prefix `claude` -> `anthropic`. So during a run with `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`, the Pass-1 batch runner replaces cfg.model with the bare `claude-haiku-4-5`, which infers provider `anthropic`. If that is what happened, the \"Bedrock\" arm of my pilot ran its Pass-1 finders against DIRECT ANTHROPIC and only the non-ladder calls went to Bedrock — making the comparison Anthropic-vs-Anthropic for the pass that does most of the work, and the agreement I reported nearly meaningless as provider evidence.\n\nWHAT I CANNOT CONCLUDE EITHER WAY. I captured only `tail -40` of the Bedrock run, so the per-call model lines for its Pass-1 are not in my log. I originally read the small number of Bedrock-named warning lines as a difference in call volume between arms; that was MY TRUNCATION, not a real asymmetry, so it is not evidence of contamination either. The honest status is: UNVERIFIED, and the pilot's PASS/PASS agreement must NOT be cited as provider parity until this is settled.\n\nWHAT THE REAL RUN MUST DO. Capture the resolved model for EVERY call in both arms (the `REBAR_USAGE_LOG` rig used by `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:83,107-119` already records per-call model) and assert that the v2 arm made ZERO calls to a non-Bedrock provider. If any bare `claude-*` ladder entry reaches a Bedrock run, that is the split-brain and it must be fixed before the corpus run, not explained afterwards.\n\nRELATED SHARP EDGE, independently confirmed: `review_kernel/verify.py:269` returns the verifier default ONLY when `model == default_model`. Any Bedrock id is a non-default value, so the Pass-2/Pass-4 sonnet downgrade STOPS APPLYING on the Bedrock arm while it still applies on the Anthropic arm. Both arms would then differ in TWO variables (provider AND per-pass model class), which makes any criterion failure unattributable and any pass unrepresentative of production. The driver must either pin both arms' per-pass models explicitly or map them per pass."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785450744743123001,"uuid":"47c07302-3eb1-4960-9e04-ae047a7fd45b"}